le f(x,y)\\le 1.$\n\n- Condition II is true. Adding up all the values of $f(x,y)$ shown in the table, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y) & =0.42+0.18+0.33+0.07=1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Condition III is true. Because $f(x,y)$ satisfies conditions I and II, it is a valid probability mass function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275143 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162063 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "38398622-ca45-5eb6-a589-96aec162960a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Joint Distribution of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2efea082-cab5-5e22-8416-01dc28335241" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272805} {:answer/id #uuid "88cad6df-9085-5a12-a539-d9298bb39155" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273566} {:answer/id #uuid "ace63423-b92d-5676-8f7c-bc3fcf46a191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273879} {:answer/id #uuid "da5d52a7-5005-5522-b1f0-e88e9eef53fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274295} {:answer/id #uuid "f777332d-8e8e-5c42-bb13-ee910d07f37d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2efea082-cab5-5e22-8416-01dc28335241" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272805} :answer-field/id #uuid "36cac13d-8d7d-510d-954b-a77def71bf38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :