begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 & -6 & -5 \\\\ -33 & 18 & 15\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(11,-33)$, $(-6,18)$ and $(-5,15).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275183 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105893 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Coordinates of an Image Formed by a Singular Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "545c7fc2-4340-581b-a776-bc17597990c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273106} {:answer/id #uuid "964c878c-3f75-5bf4-b940-59593e8a1e24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273689} {:answer/id #uuid "ae773c4b-9ecc-5b5a-8142-3e7cf1afa498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273894} {:answer/id #uuid "ccdd7e7b-1f02-5a08-9804-0d005d38236e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274170} {:answer/id #uuid "f366b36b-3e3a-501e-877c-90ccc8b61aaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f366b36b-3e3a-501e-877c-90ccc8b61aaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592